WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.360
A made-up bank makes an offer: one
hundred per cent interest a year,

2
00:00:04.410 --> 00:00:05.860
on one pound.

3
00:00:05.910 --> 00:00:10.420
Paid once, at the end of the year,
your pound becomes two pounds.

4
00:00:10.470 --> 00:00:13.840
Or take it as two payments
of fifty per cent.

5
00:00:13.890 --> 00:00:16.500
Now you end with two pounds twenty-five.

6
00:00:16.550 --> 00:00:17.720
Then quarterly.

7
00:00:17.770 --> 00:00:18.880
Then monthly.

8
00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:21.120
Paid more and more often.

9
00:00:21.170 --> 00:00:24.730
So if the bank pays ever
more often, forever,

10
00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:27.350
does your pound grow without limit?

11
00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:32.400
In this mission, you'll see why n payments
turn one pound into one plus one over

12
00:00:32.450 --> 00:00:34.270
n, to the power n.

13
00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:38.910
And you'll sketch exponential
graphs, y equals a to the x.

14
00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:42.840
Your mission: decide whether
one pound grows without limit.
